:''For the enemy encountered in [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Possessed by Evil]], see [[Evil Emperor Cat]].''
'''Emperor Cat''' is a [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Dynasty Fest (Gacha Event)|Dynasty Fest]] event. He was added in [[Version 10.10 Update|Version 10.1]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 586
|rarity = LR
|name1 = Emperor Cat
|name2 = Tyrant Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tyrant Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Emperor Cat has two main selling points: range and abilities. While he is able to outrange [[Camelle]], it is very inconsistent due to only outranging him by one. He can also provide great support against any army, thanks to his many abilities. Thus, Emperor should be used as a backline supporter, not differently than how [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]] is usually used. Protect him well and do not bother using him if you expect him to get hit a lot by [[Wave Attack|waves]], [[Surge Attack|surges]] or [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance Enemies]].

This unit has the flaw of being unreliable; though he has a 76% (or 75.99% if you want to be exact) chance of inflicting any given debuff, it's never guaranteed that what he inflicts is beneficial to the player's current needs, similarly to [[Good-Luck Ebisu (Super Rare Cat)|Good-Luck Ebisu]] and [[Mimiluga (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Mimiluga]]. On another note, his debuff downtime is 5.2 seconds without [[Fruit Treasures]]; but do not underestimate him, as he is protected by his exceptional range, making his abilities still viable.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Super-Backliner}}

