==Trivia==
*There is a substantial amount of evidence to suggest that Emperor Cat wasn't just planned to drop from [[Uncanny Legends]], but was also going to serve as a counterpart to [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]]:
**From [[Version 10.0 Update|Version 10.0]] to [[Version 10.2 Update|Version 10.2]], [[Evil Emperor Cat]]'s ID was used by a placeholder enemy named コニャンダム亜種 ''Ko Nyandamu Ashu'' ("[[Li'l Nyandam (Enemy)|Li'l Nyandam]] Variant").
**[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] and [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Possessed by Evil]]'s [[Backgrounds|background]] were also added prematurely in 10.0, but Stone Cat was a placeholder [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] instead of a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] and the background had a different colour scheme closer to that of [[Saint Red Fox]].
**These placeholders were added in the same update as [[Dawn of the Beginning]], whose Japanese name is the opposite of [[Dead End Night]]'s. Dawn of the Beginning also comes 9 sub-chapters after [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]] in [[The Gelatin Mines]], which was 9 sub-chapters after [[Depths of My Heart]].
**Emperor Cat has the same range, movement speed and slow chance as allied Li'l Nyandam while Evil Emperor Cat's Omni Strike gives him the same reach as enemy Li'l Nyandam.
**Evil Emperor Cat is a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]], the same trait as all other Uncanny Legends drops ([[Relic Bun-Bun]], [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]], [[Urs & Fenrir (Enemy)|Urs & Fenrir]], [[Elder Flame Doron]] and [[Ultima Beast Naala]]).
**Before [[Possessed Empress]] was introduced, Evil Emperor Cat stood out as the only [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] to be the enemy version of a [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]]. Likewise, Emperor Cat is to this day the only [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cat]] to have an enemy counterpart.
*The magic he uses is presumably Relic power, as it's described as [[Uncanny Legends|uncanny]] and comes from an ancient forest, and it is the mastery of this power that resulted in him becoming Evil Emperor Cat.
**If the ancient forest mentioned in his description is in fact [[Sacred Forest]], that would mean the final sub-chapter of Uncanny Legends was teased a whole 2 years before its release.
*The heads of the creatures that emerge from Tyrant Cat's portal appear to be based on [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] or [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie]].
*Emperor Cat is the only Legend Rare Cat to not use a darkened version of their icon when viewing drops for the banners he appears in.

